From 4fcf15a273653193d98776fcc56ff29498d12877 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:02:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(client): a shared game's first screen on a phone 887 ->
 719 ms, each page's chunks preloaded per route ahead of the stylesheet

The built page's preload script (vite.config.ts) stood after Vite's
stylesheet link, so the parser ran it only once the CSS had arrived, a
round trip late on a phone; and it preloaded one list on every lobby page,
the tutorial's chunks among them, and the lobby's canvas on /learn. Since
GS1 a game's address waits for its page's chunk before it first renders,
so that round trip was the first screen's. Now (ledger 1009-0411:P7):
- one table, PRELOADS: per address the page's own chunks first, then its
  canvases (three.js, the scene) at fetchPriority low, so they never hold
  the page up; no tutorial chunks on the lobby's pages, no lobby canvas on
  /learn, and ComputerGameScreen on /computer and /computer/:id;
- the script right after the viewport tag, ahead of the stylesheet;
- /computer/:id waits for its page before the app first renders, as
  /game/:id does (pageReady, screens/pageChunk.ts, which main.tsx calls;
  a part that suspends in the first commit holds it 300 ms).

Evidence: setup A/B vs fc66e8a, 6 pairs (bench/loop/ab-20261021-0649-p7.md;
scoreboard 1009-0411:P7): "A shared game's page, first screen, phone (4x CPU,
Fast 4G)" 887 -> 719 ms, x0.812, every pair 0.77-0.83, called better;
requests 25 -> 23. Desktop first screen x0.924 and first board picture
x1.004 (median pairs, mixed, not called). The same lists without the low
priority (ab-20261021-0649-p7a.md) took the phone to x0.819 but made the
desktop's first screen worse in 6 of 6 pairs (x1.074), so the scene waits.
Built per path (gzip -9 of the files linked): /game/:id and /new 425.7 ->
419.9 KB, /learn 403.5 -> 394.4 KB, /computer/:id 425.7 -> 423.9 KB with
its page now among them; the HTML 3,478 -> 3,564 B gzipped.

Checks: vite.config.test runs the generated script per address on a
hand-made bundle (fails with the tutorial's chunks back on the lobby's
pages, the computer's page dropped, or /learn's path broken), checks every
App.tsx route's row, and that GameScreen.tsx in the entry, or a scene
chunk under it, fails the build (fails with GameScreen dropped from
SHOWN_BEFORE_SCENE; ledger 1951:GT1). pageChunk.test fails with the
/game/ wait removed. Beside them, the _headers test now also expects
exactly 100 rules to pass (fails with `count >= 100`; ledger 1841:VB1). vitest 1,594 passed; e2e computer, chunkFailure and
createGame specs pass.

